- 50% → 75%: ratio goes 219.1x → 221.8x (plateau)
- 75% → 100%: ratio goes 221.8x → 245.5x

The plateau at high disorder makes sense — once the data is sufficiently disordered, insertion sort is in its O(n²) regime and the ratio approaches the random-input ratio.

